# scripts/ux-paths/UPSTREAM.sha256
#
# THE digests of the vendored copies. One file, one copy of each number.
#
# Until 2026-08-13 the same two digests were written down TWICE — in
# UPSTREAM.md and again as shell literals inside
# .github/workflows/ux-paths.yml — and nothing asserted that the two agreed.
# A re-sync that updated one and forgot the other would have left the workflow
# checking a stale number, silently, and the error message it prints told the
# next human to edit both by hand. That is a duplication with no guard, which
# is the same shape as the vendoring itself, one level down.
#
# Now the workflow reads THIS file with `sha256sum -c`. There is one place to
# update, and it is a machine-checkable format rather than a table in prose.
#
# ── the upstream commit these bytes came from ───────────────────────────────
# Recorded so that a drift report is actionable. "The bytes moved" is not
# something anybody can act on; "compare ec849d1...main" is.
#
#   upstream-repo:   devfellowship/dfl-ci
#   guard.mjs        from scripts/ux-paths-guard.mjs
#                    at ec849d10ca1c578aaa1e0c5ff095aa9e87ef7292  (2026-08-13)
#   schema-v1.json   from schema/ux-paths-v1.json
#                    at b1d688881763b5e0702960287416928f282acbfa  (2026-08-13)
#   dfl-ci HEAD when this file was written:
#                    b1d688881763b5e0702960287416928f282acbfa
#
# ⚠️ THE PIN IS A RECORD, NOT A LOCK. Nothing inside `iterahq` can read
# `devfellowship/dfl-ci` — it is private, and a private repo is readable only
# within its own org unless an enterprise widens it. `iterahq` is on the
# GitHub Free plan, so no such scope exists. The same limit is why the
# reusable workflow cannot be called and these files are vendored at all.
# GitHub reports the cross-org miss as 404, not 403, so the failure disguises
# itself as "repository not found".
#
# The check that upstream has not moved therefore runs FROM THE OTHER SIDE:
# devfellowship/dfl-ci:.github/workflows/ux-paths-vendor-drift.yml reads this
# file daily and opens an issue here when the digests no longer match its own.
# That job holds the credential, because devfellowship is the org that has one
# that reaches both.
#
# ── re-syncing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   gh api repos/devfellowship/dfl-ci/contents/scripts/ux-paths-guard.mjs?ref=<sha> \
#     --jq .content | base64 -d > scripts/ux-paths/guard.mjs
#   sha256sum scripts/ux-paths/guard.mjs      # update the line below
#   # update the pinned sha above, in the same pull request
#
# Format below is exactly `sha256sum` output, so `sha256sum -c` reads it.

4d744547ee5dc100393e73e8a8217aa9fbb15c28b2982c4a266552c2ae490722  scripts/ux-paths/guard.mjs
ac8b8c6bda1e8f19c266002e92c749100e839b02a142670a0509b4bcf53e542e  scripts/ux-paths/schema-v1.json
